WEBVTT

00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:13,470
What are your thoughts on using colostrum with growth factors

00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:18,210
for someone with hormone-positive breast cancer?

00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:22,690
Clostrum is a common supplement these days

00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:26,330
and colostrum does have growth factors.

00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:33,450
Clostrum is going to be a dairy-based product.

00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,130
And it does have growth factors,

00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,690
and that's really the benefit of it.

00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:40,130
It can help heal your gutted things.

00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:43,690
So it's typically not recommended for anybody

00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:46,530
with any type of cancer.

00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:49,330
Now, if you had to take colostrum for a short period time

00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,770
to help with something else, I don't

00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:54,810
see that as a real problem.

00:00:54,810 --> 00:00:59,890
But to be honest, while you're in the throes of cancer,

00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:02,130
there can be dangers to that.

00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:06,050
Now, I would say also that if it depends

00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:09,530
on where you're at with your cancer with any of these two,

00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:12,250
even with glutamine, let's say your cancer is in full remission,

00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:14,770
which you have really damaged gut.

00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:18,290
And you want to take glutamine for a short period of time.

00:01:18,290 --> 00:01:19,450
Is it OK to do that?

00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:22,010
Well, yes, probably.

00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:23,970
I mean, there's no way to absolutely know

00:01:23,970 --> 00:01:27,810
whether it's going to be a perfect situation for anybody.

00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:30,530
But using common sense, if you're

00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:33,290
trying to accomplish another task with a product

00:01:33,290 --> 00:01:34,690
for a short period of time, if you're going

00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:37,050
to take colostrum because you've read this thing,

00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:39,370
they'd be really good for you.

00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:42,850
And you want to be on it on a regular basis.

00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:45,530
If your cancer is a complete remission,

00:01:45,530 --> 00:01:48,010
then I would think twice about that.

00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:51,810
But if your cancer wasn't complete remission,

00:01:51,810 --> 00:01:53,490
you were doing really well, but now you're

00:01:53,490 --> 00:01:57,050
trying to heal something else, testing it out

00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:59,010
and going out at a first short period of time.

00:01:59,010 --> 00:02:00,810
I don't see that as a big problem.

